STRINGS (ADR-014) — zero hardcoded literals. The Android res/values*/strings.xml catalog is GENERATED
from web/src/i18n (gen-i18n.ts, with a --check drift gate); web i18n is outside this artifact's allowed
files, so ONLY pre-existing generated keys are referenced (no new keys, no drift). Keys used:
  glance.noVehicle ("No vehicle found")    glance.action.lock / glance.action.unlock
  glance.action.climateOn / climateOff     common.sentry            a11y.loading
  widget.charging   widget.timeToFull      widget.commandSuccess / widget.commandFailed   common.retry
  freshness.justNow / seconds / minutes / hours / days / weeks   (last-updated relative age)
The coarse state shown in the badge is backend DATA (data.state), rendered verbatim as on the web — not a
UI literal. SI display values come from the shared UnitFormatter (P1/S5), never hardcoded units.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY-SCOPE NOTES (honesty covenant #2 — no scope narrowing)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Data sources bound (manifest page:watch/WatchFace): useWatchSummary (GET /watch/summary, the glance feed,
  loading→success→empty→error) and useWatchCommand (POST /watch/command, the lock/climate quick-action
  dispatch with an outcome snackbar). Both route through the shared S7 WatchRepository (P1/S2-S3, ADR-004).
- Panels/charts/maps: the manifest extracts NONE (the web page renders no <GlassPanel>/chart/map). Every
  region of the chrome-less <WatchShell> is reproduced in the same data + grouping + order: vehicle name →
  battery gauge (+ charging + state badge) → quick actions (lock/climate/sentry) → last-updated.
- The web page also renders an OPT-IN Helix narrator <AIWatchFaceNLResponse /> as a sibling that returns
  null in the default AI-off mode (the wearable invariant). That narrator binds the `useAiStream` data
  source — NOT one of THIS unit's data sources — and is a SEPARATE shared-surface parity unit
  (com/teslasync/shared-surfaces/AIWatchFaceNLResponse, with its own tests). It is therefore covered there,
  not embedded here; the chrome-less shell is the canonical baseline every user sees, exactly as web off-mode.

